{
"type": "short",
"q_en": "Explain why a protein with a single oxygen-binding site could not do haemoglobin's job, using the actual partial pressures involved.",
"q_cn": "请用实际涉及的分压数值，解释为什么一个只有单一氧结合位点的蛋白质无法完成血红蛋白的工作。",
"accept": [
"13.3",
"4 kPa",
"sigmoid",
"cooperativity",
"T state",
"R state",
"S形",
"协同",
"双曲线"
],
"answer_en": "Haemoglobin must load oxygen in the lungs at a pO2 of about 13.3 kilopascals and unload it in the tissues at about 4 kilopascals. A protein with one binding site gives a hyperbolic curve and therefore has a single fixed affinity. If that affinity is high it will load efficiently in the lungs but release very little in the tissues; if it is low it will release in the tissues but pick up little in the lungs. No single affinity satisfies both requirements. Haemoglobin escapes the dilemma by not having one affinity: it converts from the low-affinity T state to the high-affinity R state as successive oxygen molecules bind, so the first O2 binds weakly to a T-state subunit while the fourth binds to a subunit already in R, and the resulting curve is sigmoid rather than hyperbolic. That shape makes the protein far more sensitive to the difference between 13.3 and 4 kilopascals. Lehninger states the constraint explicitly: a single-subunit protein with a single ligand-binding site cannot produce a sigmoid binding curve even if binding elicits a conformational change, because each molecule binds independently and cannot affect another.",
"answer_cn": "血红蛋白必须在肺部约13.3千帕的pO2下装载氧，并在组织中约4千帕下卸载。只有一个结合位点的蛋白质给出双曲线型曲线，因而只有单一固定的亲和力。若该亲和力高，它在肺部能高效装载，却在组织中几乎不释放；若该亲和力低，它在组织中能释放，却在肺部装不上多少。没有任何单一亲和力能同时满足这两项要求。血红蛋白摆脱这一两难的办法是「不具有单一亲和力」：随着一个个氧分子结合，它由低亲和力的T态转变为高亲和力的R态，因此第一个O2弱结合到处于T态的亚基上，而第四个则结合到已处于R态的亚基上，由此得到的曲线呈S形而非双曲线。这个形状使该蛋白质对13.3千帕与4千帕之间的差别敏感得多。Lehninger明确陈述了这一约束：具有单一配体结合位点的单亚基蛋白质无法产生S形结合曲线，即使结合能引发构象变化也不行，因为每个分子的结合都是独立的，无法影响另一个分子。"
}
