"why_en": "The sentence that changes the picture is short and blunt: “ Vitamin D3 is not itself biologically active, but it is converted by enzymes in the liver and kidney to ” the compound printed as 1-alpha,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3, calcitriol, “ a hormone that regulates calcium uptake in the intestine and calcium levels in kidney and bone ” , with the liver adding a hydroxyl at C-25 and the kidney a second one at C-1 (A p.357, **figure** 10-19). So the pathway is skin, then liver, then kidney, then nucleus — calcitriol regulates gene expression by interacting with specific nuclear receptor proteins. Deficiency gives defective bone formation and rickets. Vitamin D2, ergocalciferol, is made commercially by UV irradiation of yeast ergosterol, differs only slightly in the side chain on the sterol D ring, has the same biological effects, and is what is added to milk and butter.",
"why_cn": "**改变整幅图景的那句话又短又硬**：**「vitamin D3 本身没有生物活性，但它被肝和肾中的酶转化为 1α,25-二羟基维生素 D3（calcitriol）——一个调节肠道钙吸收以及肾和骨中钙水平的激素」**；**肝在 C-25 上加一个羟基，肾在 C-1 上加第二个**（A 第 357 页，**figure** 10-19）。**所以这条路线是：皮肤 → 肝 → 肾 → 细胞核**——**calcitriol 通过与特定核受体蛋白相互作用来调节基因表达**。**缺乏会导致骨形成缺陷与佝偻病。** **Vitamin D2（ergocalciferol）由酵母 ergosterol 经紫外照射商业化生产**，**仅在固醇 D 环的侧链上略有不同**，**生物学效应相同**，**它就是被加进牛奶和黄油里的那一个。**"
