"why_en": "The sentence is precise about which group is the head and what the body includes: “ Cholesterol, the major sterol in animal tissues, is amphipathic, with a polar head group (the hydroxyl group at C-3) and a nonpolar hydrocarbon body (the steroid nucleus and the hydrocarbon side chain at C-17) about as long as a 16-carbon fatty acid in its extended form ” (A p.352). One oxygen atom against twenty-odd carbons is the smallest polar head of any lipid in the chapter, and the length calibration against a C16 acid is what lets you picture cholesterol lying alongside a phospholipid tail with its hydroxyl reaching the aqueous surface. **Figure** 10-15's caption adds the corollary: for storage and transport, that same hydroxyl condenses with a fatty acid to form a sterol ester, which removes the amphipathy entirely.",
"why_cn": "**这句话对「哪个基团是头」和「身体包含什么」都说得很准**：**「胆固醇是动物组织的主要固醇，它是两亲的：极性头基是 C-3 上的羟基，非极性的烃身体是甾核加上 C-17 上的烃侧链，后者在伸展形态下大约与一个十六碳脂肪酸等长。」**（A 第 352 页）。**一个氧原子对着二十来个碳，是本章所有脂质里最小的极性头**；**而「以 C16 酸校准长度」这一点，正是让你能想象出胆固醇贴着一条磷脂尾巴躺下、把羟基伸到水相表面的依据**。****figure** 10-15 的图注补上了推论**：**为了储存与运输，同一个羟基与一个脂肪酸缩合形成固醇酯**——**而这就把两亲性完全去掉了。**"
