"why_en": "Lehninger states the target and lists the consequence: prednisone's anti-inflammatory activity is “ mediated in part by the inhibition of arachidonate release by phospholipase A2 and consequent inhibition of the synthesis of prostaglandins, thromboxanes, leukotrienes, and lipoxins ” (A p.356). All four classes are named because all four are made from arachidonate, and arachidonate has to be released from the C-2 position of a membrane glycerophospholipid before any of them can be built — which is precisely what phospholipase A2 does, and precisely the enzyme Czech 8-4-2-1 places at sn-2 on its phosphatidylcholine diagram. An NSAID such as aspirin acts further down: cyclooxygenase catalyses an early step from arachidonate to the series 2 prostaglandins and thromboxanes only, so leukotrienes and lipoxins survive it. That level difference is why prednisone reaches asthma, which is leukotriene-driven. Note Lehninger's hedge — in part — and do not present this as the whole mechanism.",
"why_cn": "**Lehninger 点出了靶点，并列出了后果**：prednisone 的抗炎活性**「其作用部分是通过抑制 phospholipase A2 释放 arachidonate、并因而抑制 prostaglandin、thromboxane、leukotriene 和 lipoxin 的合成来实现的」**（A 第 356 页）。**四类全被点名，因为四类都由 arachidonate 造出来**；而**arachidonate 必须先从膜甘油磷脂的 C-2 位释放出来，任何一类才谈得上被合成**——**而这正是 phospholipase A2 干的事**，**也正是捷克 `8-4-2-1` 在它的 phosphatidylcholine 图上标在 sn-2 位置的那个酶**。**阿司匹林这类 NSAID 作用在更下游**：**cyclooxygenase 只催化从 arachidonate 通向 2 系列 prostaglandin 和 thromboxane 的早期一步**，**所以 leukotriene 和 lipoxin 能挺过去**。**这个层级差别，正是 prednisone 能管到（由 leukotriene 驱动的）哮喘的原因。** **注意 Lehninger 的限定词「部分」**——**不要把它讲成全部机制。**"
