"why_en": "The amplification is the whole point. Cells normally have a far higher concentration of ATP (5 to 10 mM) than of AMP (under 0.1 mM), and when ATP is consumed AMP is produced in two steps: hydrolysis gives ADP, then adenylate kinase runs 2 ADP to AMP + ATP. Because AMP starts from a low base, Table 13-11 shows ATP falling 5.0 to 4.5 mM (10%) while AMP rises 0.1 to 0.6 mM (600%), with ADP unchanged. The reader is AMP-activated protein kinase, AMPK, which AMP activates allosterically and which the book explicitly distinguishes from the cyclic AMP-dependent protein kinase PKA. Option 2 invents a diffusion argument and names the wrong kinase — the book warns against exactly that confusion. Option 3 invents chemical stability and misassigns the reader role to adenylate kinase, which produces AMP rather than responding to it. Option 4 invents a competitive-inhibition mechanism the section does not describe.",
"why_cn": "**那份放大效应就是全部要点。** **细胞平时的 ATP 浓度（5 到 10 mM）远高于 AMP（低于 0.1 mM）**；**当 ATP 被消耗时，AMP 分两步生成：水解先给出 ADP，随后 adenylate kinase 跑 2 ADP → AMP + ATP**。**因为 AMP 的基线很低，Table 13-11 显示 ATP 由 5.0 降到 4.5 mM（10%），而 AMP 由 0.1 升到 0.6 mM（600%），ADP 则保持不变**。**读取它的是 AMP-activated protein kinase（AMPK）**，**AMP 以别构方式激活它**；**教材明确把它与依赖 cAMP 的蛋白激酶 PKA 区分开**。**选项 2** 凭空发明了一个扩散论证，并且点错了激酶——**教材恰恰警告过这个混淆**。**选项 3** 凭空发明了化学稳定性，还把「读取者」的角色错派给了 adenylate kinase——**后者是生成 AMP 的，不是响应 AMP 的**。**选项 4** 凭空发明了一个本节并未描述的竞争性抑制机制。"
