"why_en": "The catalytic subunit of PP1 does not exist free in the cytosol but is tightly bound to its target proteins through a tissue-specific regulatory subunit, one of a family of glycogen-targeting proteins that bind glycogen and each of the three enzymes: GM in muscle, GL in liver. On top of that it is gated four ways: inactivated when phosphorylated by PKA, activated allosterically by glucose 6-phosphate, blocked by phosphorylated inhibitor 1, and directly inhibited by active glycogen phosphorylase — that last one being a futile-cycle interlock built from the pathway itself (A p.568).",
"why_cn": "PP1 的催化亚基不以游离形式存在于胞质中，而是通过一个组织特异的调节亚基紧紧结合在它的靶蛋白上——那是一族糖原靶向蛋白之一，它们既结合糖原，也结合那三个酶：肌肉里是 GM，肝里是 GL。在此之上还有四道闸：被 PKA 磷酸化而失活、被 glucose 6-phosphate 别构激活、被磷酸化的 inhibitor 1 阻断、并被有活性的 glycogen phosphorylase 直接抑制——最后这一条正是用通路自己的零件搭出来的无效循环联锁（A 第 568 页）。"
