"why_en": "“Two ATP molecules are required to make carbamoyl phosphate, and one ATP to make argininosuccinate — the latter ATP undergoing a pyrophosphate cleavage to AMP and PPi, which is hydrolyzed to two Pi” (A p.638). Three ATP molecules go in, but the third is split to AMP rather than to ADP, so restoring it to ATP requires two phosphorylations instead of one: that step alone spends two high-energy bonds, and 2 plus 2 is four. This is exactly the point Czech node 5-2-2-2 already makes, and the two layers agree. The half that node does not have is what Lehninger says next: considered **in isolation** the cost is four, but the fumarate leaving the cycle becomes malate, enters the mitochondrion, and yields an NADH worth up to 2.5 ATP, greatly reducing the real cost.",
"why_cn": "**「两分子 ATP 用于生成氨甲酰磷酸，一分子 ATP 用于生成精氨基琥珀酸——后面这个 ATP 经历的是焦磷酸裂解，生成 AMP 和 PPi，而 PPi 再被水解成两个 Pi。」**（A 印刷页 638）**进去的是三个 ATP 分子**，但**第三个被切成的是 AMP 而不是 ADP**，所以把它恢复成 ATP 需要**两次磷酸化而不是一次**：**这一步自己就花掉两根高能键**，2 加 2 等于 **4**。这正是捷克节点 5-2-2-2 已经讲过的那一点，**两层完全一致**。那个节点没有的另一半，是 Lehninger 紧接着说的：**「孤立地看」代价是四个**，但**离开循环的延胡索酸变成苹果酸、进入线粒体、产出最多值 2.5 个 ATP 的 NADH，大幅降低了真实代价。**"
