"why_en": "“There is no transporter to directly move the fumarate generated in cytosolic arginine synthesis back into the mitochondrial matrix. However, fumarate can be converted to malate in the cytosol” (A p.636). That conversion is available because fumarase and malate dehydrogenase both exist as cytosolic isozymes as well as mitochondrial ones, and malate has a carrier, the malate-alpha-ketoglutarate transporter. The consequence for a drawn diagram is concrete: fumarate to malate in the cytosol, malate across the membrane, and only then back into the citric acid cycle. This whole link is the aspartate-argininosuccinate shunt, and the two cycles together are the Krebs bicycle — though Lehninger stresses that each cycle can still operate independently.",
"why_cn": "**「不存在能把胞质中精氨酸合成所产生的延胡索酸直接搬回线粒体基质的转运体。不过，延胡索酸可以在胞质中被转成苹果酸。」**（A 印刷页 636）这条转换之所以可行，是因为**延胡索酸酶和苹果酸脱氢酶除线粒体型外还各有胞质同工酶**，而**苹果酸有载体**——**苹果酸-alpha-酮戊二酸转运体**。对着黑板画图时的后果是具体的：**胞质里延胡索酸 → 苹果酸，苹果酸过膜，然后才回到柠檬酸循环。** 这整条连接就是 **aspartate–argininosuccinate shunt**，而两个循环合起来叫 **Krebs bicycle**——尽管 Lehninger 强调**每个循环仍能独立运转**。"
