"answer": 1,
"why_en": "Both halves of the question are answered by the same structural fact: this genome is present in many copies per cell, and it comes from one parent. Because a typical cell has hundreds or thousands of mitochondria and each holds about five copies of the genome, a mutation is present as a fraction rather than as a yes or a no. A defective mitochondrion in a germ cell replicates alongside normal ones and its progeny are randomly distributed to daughter cells, so mature eggs end up with different proportions of defective mitochondria, and after fertilisation the somatic cells of the embryo differ in their proportion of mutant mitochondria. That is heteroplasmy, defined against homoplasmy, in which every mitochondrial genome in every cell is the same. Individuals with the same mtDNA mutation may therefore have symptoms of differing severity, depending on the number and distribution of affected mitochondria -- so genotype does not predict phenotype here, the dose and its tissue distribution do. The father's irrelevance is the second half: animals inherit essentially all of their mitochondria from the female parent, for two reasons that compound. Eggs are large and contain 10^5 or 10^6 mitochondria while sperm are much smaller and contain far fewer, perhaps 100 to 1,000; and beyond that dilution there is an active mechanism, in which maternal phagosomes migrate to the site of sperm entry just after fertilisation, engulf the sperm mitochondria and degrade them. So an affected mother can transmit to all her children and an affected father to none, and that asymmetry identifies a mitochondrial pedigree before any sequencing is done.",
"why_cn": "问题的两半由同一个结构性事实回答：**这个基因组在每个细胞里有很多份，而且它只来自一方亲本。** 因为典型细胞有**几百到几千个**线粒体、每个又装**约五份**基因组拷贝，所以一个突变是以**一个比例**、而不是以「有/无」的形式存在的。生殖细胞里一个有缺陷的线粒体会**和正常线粒体一起复制**，其后代**被随机分配**到子细胞中，于是成熟卵细胞各自含有**不同比例**的缺陷线粒体；受精之后，胚胎的体细胞在**突变型线粒体所占比例**上彼此不同。这就是 **heteroplasmy**，它是相对 **homoplasmy**（每个细胞里每一份线粒体基因组都相同）定义的。所以**带同一个 mtDNA 突变的个体，症状严重程度可以各不相同**，取决于**受累线粒体的数量与分布**——**在这里基因型不预测表型，「剂量」和它的组织分布才预测表型。** 父亲的「无关」是第二半：**动物的线粒体基本上全部继承自母本**，原因有两条且互相叠加。**卵子很大，含 10⁵ 或 10⁶ 个线粒体；精子小得多，所含少得多，大约 100–1,000 个**；而在这种稀释之上还有一套**主动机制**——受精刚发生之后，**母源 phagosome 迁移到精子进入的位点，把精子线粒体吞入并降解**。所以**患病的母亲可以传给她所有子女，患病的父亲一个也不传**；**光凭这条不对称，在任何测序之前就能认出一份线粒体系谱。**"
