"why_en": "A p.1040. Corynebacterium diphtheriae releases diphtheria toxin (Mr 58,330), which catalyses “the ADP-ribosylation of a diphthamide (a modified histidine) residue of eukaryotic elongation factor eEF2”, thereby inactivating it Since eEF2 is the eukaryotic counterpart of bacterial EF-G, the translocase, the cell can no longer move the ribosome along the message and translation stops. The dead cells form the thick grey membrane over throat and tonsils that gives the disease its clinical signature. Ricin (Mr 29,895) is the other toxin aimed at us, inactivating the 60S subunit by depurinating a specific adenosine in 28S rRNA.",
"why_cn": "A 印刷页 1040。白喉棒状杆菌释放**白喉毒素**（Mr 58,330），它**催化真核延长因子 eEF2 上一个 diphthamide（一种修饰过的组氨酸）残基的 ADP-核糖基化，从而使其失活**。由于 **eEF2 就是细菌 EF-G（移位酶）在真核里的对应物**，细胞再也无法把核糖体沿信息推进，**翻译因此停止**。死掉的细胞在咽喉与扁桃体上形成那层厚的灰色假膜，正是这个病的临床标志。**蓖麻毒素**（Mr 29,895）是另一个冲着我们来的毒素，它**通过把 28S rRNA 上一个特定腺苷去嘌呤化**使 **60S 亚基**失活。"
